00:11:36,498 --> 00:11:39,187
pay, which includes trust in the brand.

279
00:11:39,367 --> 00:11:42,613
Longevity measures how many trucks reach a

280
00:11:42,613 --> 00:11:46,400
high mileage, which includes trucks with replaced

281
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,018
engines.

282
00:11:47,198 --> 00:11:50,890
And the reliability ranking measures problems,

283
00:11:50,890 --> 00:11:52,817
recalls and repair cost.

284
00:11:52,997 --> 00:11:55,292
A truck can be trusted by the

285
00:11:55,292 --> 00:11:57,270
market, last a long time,

286
00:11:57,270 --> 00:11:59,802
and still have a serious flaw on

287
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,147
some model years.

288
00:12:01,327 --> 00:12:03,440
That is what the Tundra is.

289
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:06,527
So who should buy a twenty twenty-seven

290
00:12:06,527 --> 00:12:07,018
Tundra?

291
00:12:07,198 --> 00:12:09,240
A buyer who values resale,

292
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:11,832
who keeps trucks for a long time,

293
00:12:11,832 --> 00:12:14,659
and who accepts that Toyota has said

294
00:12:14,659 --> 00:12:18,193
the manufacturing problem has been addressed.

295
00:12:18,373 --> 00:12:20,802
Also a buyer who wants a hybrid

296
00:12:20,802 --> 00:12:22,056
with real power,

297
00:12:22,056 --> 00:12:23,388
and the inverter.

298
00:12:23,568 --> 00:12:24,869
And who should wait?

299
00:12:25,049 --> 00:12:27,057
A buyer who wants proof.

300
00:12:27,237 --> 00:12:29,975
Because a twenty twenty-seven truck has no

301
00:12:29,975 --> 00:12:31,083
track record yet,

302
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:34,147
and the twenty twenty-two to twenty twenty-four

303
00:12:34,147 --> 00:12:36,363
trucks are the ones with the known

304
00:12:36,363 --> 00:12:36,885
problem.

305
00:12:37,234 --> 00:12:39,005
And if you are shopping for a

306
00:12:39,005 --> 00:12:41,263
used Tundra, the advice is different.

307
00:12:41,443 --> 00:12:43,774
Check the build date of the exact

308
00:12:43,774 --> 00:12:46,740
truck, and check whether the recall repair

309
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:47,376
was done.

310
00:12:47,556 --> 00:12:49,954
A twenty twenty-two to twenty twenty-four truck

311
00:12:49,954 --> 00:12:51,740
that has had a documented repair is

312
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:53,679
a different purchase from one that has

313
00:12:53,679 --> 00:12:53,883
not.

314
00:12:54,063 --> 00:12:55,596
Ask for the paperwork.

315
00:12:55,776 --> 00:12:58,097
A Toyota dealer can look up the

316
00:12:58,097 --> 00:13:02,067
recall status with the vehicle identification number,

317
00:13:02,067 --> 00:13:04,089
and it takes a few minutes.

318
00:13:04,438 --> 00:13:06,702
Let us slow down on the recall,

319
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:09,477
because this is the part that confuses

320
00:13:09,477 --> 00:13:09,988
people.

321
00:13:10,168 --> 00:13:12,608
A recall is not the same as

322
00:13:12,608 --> 00:13:13,512
a verdict.

323
00:13:13,692 --> 00:13:15,745
It means the manufacturer,

324
00:13:15,745 --> 00:13:17,166
or the government,

325
00:13:17,166 --> 00:13:20,483
identified a defect that can affect safety

326
00:13:20,483 --> 00:13:23,325
or function, and a repair is offered

327
00:13:23,325 --> 00:13:25,220
at no cost to the owner.

328
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:27,246
It does not tell you how many

329
00:13:27,246 --> 00:13:28,709
trucks actually failed.

330
00:13:28,889 --> 00:13:30,873
And it does not tell you whether

331
00:13:30,873 --> 00:13:32,546
a repaired truck will last.

332
00:13:32,726 --> 00:13:35,303
So the right question is not whether

333
00:13:35,303 --> 00:13:36,662
there was a recall.

334
00:13:36,842 --> 00:13:39,055
It is whether this exact truck was

335
00:13:39,055 --> 00:13:39,640
repaired.

336
00:13:39,990 --> 00:13:41,233
Here is how to check.

337
00:13:41,413 --> 00:13:44,859
Every truck has a seventeen character vehicle

338
00:13:44,859 --> 00:13:48,459
identification number, found on the driver side

339
00:13:48,459 --> 00:13:50,910
of the dashboard and on the door

340
00:13:50,910 --> 00:13:51,293
jamb.

341
00:13:51,473 --> 00:13:55,535
The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration lets

342
00:13:55,535 --> 00:13:58,047
you type that number on its recall

343
00:13:58,047 --> 00:14:00,854
website and see open recalls for free.

344
00:14:01,034 --> 00:14:03,613
A Toyota dealer can also look it

345
00:14:03,613 --> 00:14:03,855
up.

346
00:14:04,035 --> 00:14:05,893
If a recall is open,

347
00:14:05,893 --> 00:14:07,657
the repair is free.

348
00:14:07,837 --> 00:14:09,094
If it was done,

349
00:14:09,094 --> 00:14:10,937
ask for the paperwork.

350
00:14:11,117 --> 00:14:12,747
This takes five minutes,

351
00:14:12,747 --> 00:14:15,192
and it matters more than any review.

352
00:14:15,542 --> 00:14:17,830
Now the question about the hybrid.

353
00:14:18,010 --> 00:14:21,609
The i-Force Max has forty-eight more horsepower

354
00:14:21,609 --> 00:14:24,749
and one hundred four more pound-feet than

355
00:14:24,749 --> 00:14:26,205
the standard V six,

356
00:14:26,205 --> 00:14:27,507
and the inverter.

357
00:14:27,687 --> 00:14:29,424
But it adds complexity,

358
00:14:29,424 --> 00:14:31,616
a battery and electric motor,

359
00:14:31,616 --> 00:14:33,882
and the sources we used do not

360
00:14:33,882 --> 00:14:37,207
give the extra cost for twenty twenty-seven.

361
00:14:37,387 --> 00:14:39,964
So the honest advice is simple.

362
00:14:40,144 --> 00:14:41,914
If you tow heavy loads,

363
00:14:41,914 --> 00:14:43,991
or want to power tools on a

364
00:14:43,991 --> 00:14:46,530
job site, the hybrid makes sense.

365
00:14:46,710 --> 00:14:49,235
If you drive mostly on roads with

366
00:14:49,235 --> 00:14:52,219
light loads, the standard V six already

367
00:14:52,219 --> 00:14:55,356
has three hundred eighty-nine horsepower,

368
00:14:55,356 --> 00:14:56,810
and that is plenty.

369
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,487
It also helps to read the longevity

370
00:14:59,487 --> 00:15:00,551
study carefully.

371
00:15:00,731 --> 00:15:03,345
A truck can reach two hundred fifty

372
00:15:03,345 --> 00:15:06,857
thousand miles because the engine is excellent,

373
00:15:06,857 --> 00:15:09,770
or because an owner replaced the engine

374
00:15:09,770 --> 00:15:11,040
and kept driving.

375
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:13,303
The study counts miles,

376
00:15:13,303 --> 00:15:14,843
not repair bills.

377
00:15:15,023 --> 00:15:17,879
And resale value measures what the market

378
00:15:17,879 --> 00:15:18,924
believes today.

379
00:15:19,104 --> 00:15:20,876
If the market is wrong about a

380
00:15:20,876 --> 00:15:23,063
problem, the price will change later.

381
00:15:23,243 --> 00:15:25,744
So use these numbers as signals,

382
00:15:25,744 --> 00:15:27,151
not as guarantees,

383
00:15:27,151 --> 00:15:30,200
and never as a replacement for checking

384
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,451
the exact truck.

385
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:34,599
One more point for buyers who finance.

386
00:15:34,779 --> 00:15:37,296
A truck that holds eighty percent of

387
00:15:37,296 --> 00:15:39,393
its value helps you when it is

388
00:15:39,393 --> 00:15:40,932
time to sell or trade.

389
00:15:41,112 --> 00:15:42,964
But the price you pay at the

390
00:15:42,964 --> 00:15:44,618
start still matters most.

391
00:15:44,798 --> 00:15:46,564
At the estimates we saw,

392
00:15:46,564 --> 00:15:49,654
a Tundra can cost from forty-five thousand

393
00:15:49,654 --> 00:15:52,008
to eighty-four thousand dollars.

394
00:15:52,188 --> 00:15:54,733
Every thousand dollars you pay above the

395
00:15:54,733 --> 00:15:57,151
average is a thousand dollars you need

396
00:15:57,151 --> 00:15:58,805
the resale value to cover.

397
00:15:58,985 --> 00:16:01,115
So compare the same trim,

398
00:16:01,115 --> 00:16:02,563
the same options,

399
00:16:02,563 --> 00:16:04,011
and the same day,

400
00:16:04,011 --> 00:16:06,567
across at least three dealers.

401
00:16:06,917 --> 00:16:09,639
Let us put the three Tundra measures

402
00:16:09,639 --> 00:16:11,681
side by side one more time,

403
00:16:11,681 --> 00:16:14,781
because buyers often remember only one of

404
00:16:14,781 --> 00:16:15,160
them.

405
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:19,090
Resale is eighty and three tenths percent

406
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:20,645
after five years.

407
00:16:20,825 --> 00:16:24,528
Longevity is twenty-eight point two percent reaching

408
00:16:24,528 --> 00:16:26,878
two hundred fifty thousand miles,

409
00:16:26,878 --> 00:16:28,302
second in the study.

410
00:16:28,482 --> 00:16:32,369
And Pickup Truck Talk ranked reliability fifth

411
00:16:32,369 --> 00:16:33,045
of five.

412
00:16:33,225 --> 00:16:35,488
If you only heard the first two,

413
00:16:35,488 --> 00:16:37,822
you would think there is no risk.

414
00:16:38,002 --> 00:16:39,882
If you only heard the third,

415
00:16:39,882 --> 00:16:42,165
you would think there is no reason

416
00:16:42,165 --> 00:16:42,635
to buy.

417
00:16:42,815 --> 00:16:44,603
Both views are incomplete.

418
00:16:44,953 --> 00:16:47,294
What does the engine problem mean for

419
00:16:47,294 --> 00:16:48,749
a buyer of a new truck?

420
00:16:48,929 --> 00:16:51,264
It means the question has moved from

421
00:16:51,264 --> 00:16:53,923
whether the problem existed to whether it

422
00:16:53,923 --> 00:16:54,571
was fixed.

423
00:16:54,751 --> 00:16:58,415
Toyota says the manufacturing problem has been

424
00:16:58,415 --> 00:17:02,317
addressed, and recall documents say engines built

425
00:17:02,317 --> 00:17:05,741
after the changes fall outside the affected

426
00:17:05,741 --> 00:17:07,174
production period.

427
00:17:07,354 --> 00:17:09,316
That is a statement from the maker.

428
00:17:09,496 --> 00:17:11,528
It is not independent proof.

429
00:17:11,708 --> 00:17:12,987
So for a new truck,

430
00:17:12,987 --> 00:17:15,073
the sensible step is to ask the

431
00:17:15,073 --> 00:17:17,495
dealer to put the warranty terms for

432
00:17:17,495 --> 00:17:18,976
the engine in writing.

433
00:17:19,326 --> 00:17:21,502
When you test drive a Tundra,

434
00:17:21,502 --> 00:17:22,553
use your ears.

435
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:25,942
The problem described in the article could

436
00:17:25,942 --> 00:17:29,304
cause knocking, rough running or power loss.

437
00:17:29,484 --> 00:17:31,605
So drive the truck cold if you

438
00:17:31,605 --> 00:17:33,797
can, ask the dealer not to warm

439
00:17:33,797 --> 00:17:35,494
it up before you arrive,

440
00:17:35,494 --> 00:17:37,756
and listen at startup and at low

441
00:17:37,756 --> 00:17:38,180
speed.

442
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,056
Take it on a road where you

443
00:17:40,056 --> 00:17:41,437
can accelerate firmly.

444
00:17:41,617 --> 00:17:44,121
A test drive does not prove an

445
00:17:44,121 --> 00:17:45,457
engine is sound,

446
00:17:45,457 --> 00:17:47,794
but a rough start or a knock

447
00:17:47,794 --> 00:17:50,382
is a clear reason to walk away.

448
00:17:50,733 --> 00:17:52,678
Now the subscription issue,

449
00:17:52,678 --> 00:17:54,912
because it is easy to overlook.

450
00:17:55,092 --> 00:17:57,888
The digital key needs an active Remote

451
00:17:57,888 --> 00:18:00,096
Connect trial or subscription.

452
00:18:00,276 --> 00:18:01,564
Before you sign,

453
00:18:01,564 --> 00:18:03,576
ask what the trial lasts,

454
00:18:03,576 --> 00:18:05,990
what the plan costs afterward,

455
00:18:05,990 --> 00:18:08,404
and what happens to the key if

456
00:18:08,404 --> 00:18:09,692
you stop paying.

457
00:18:09,872 --> 00:18:12,466
Our sources do not give those answers,

458
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:13,900
so we will not guess.

459
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:15,694
The point is simple.

460
00:18:15,874 --> 00:18:18,024
A feature that is standard on the

461
00:18:18,024 --> 00:18:20,370
window sticker may still depend on a

462
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:21,412
monthly service.

463
00:18:21,763 --> 00:18:24,839
The towing numbers also deserve a practical

464
00:18:24,839 --> 00:18:25,269
check.

465
00:18:25,449 --> 00:18:28,868
CarGurus said up to twelve thousand pounds,

466
00:18:28,868 --> 00:18:32,367
and Kelley Blue Book showed eleven thousand,

467
00:18:32,367 --> 00:18:33,878
four hundred fifty.

468
00:18:34,058 --> 00:18:36,412
Neither figure is a promise about the

469
00:18:36,412 --> 00:18:37,494
truck on the lot.

470
00:18:37,674 --> 00:18:39,952
The sticker on the driver door jamb

471
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:42,426
lists the weight limits for that exact

472
00:18:42,426 --> 00:18:45,224
vehicle, and the payload there includes the

473
00:18:45,224 --> 00:18:46,136
weight of you,

474
00:18:46,136 --> 00:18:48,088
your passengers and your gear.

475
00:18:48,268 --> 00:18:50,210
If you tow a trailer often,

476
00:18:50,210 --> 00:18:52,583
do that math before you decide on

477
00:18:52,583 --> 00:18:53,086
a trim.

478
00:18:53,437 --> 00:18:56,299
Consider also what the inverter would do

479
00:18:56,299 --> 00:18:57,802
for you in daily use.

480
00:18:57,982 --> 00:19:01,416
A two point four kilowatt inverter can

481
00:19:01,416 --> 00:19:04,127
run power tools at a job site,

482
00:19:04,127 --> 00:19:06,025
lights at a campsite,

483
00:19:06,025 --> 00:19:09,278
or a few essentials in an emergency.

484
00:19:09,458 --> 00:19:11,811
But Toyota has not said where the

485
00:19:11,811 --> 00:19:14,448
outlets are or whether full output is

486
00:19:14,448 --> 00:19:16,088
available while parked.

487
00:19:16,268 --> 00:19:18,304
So do not buy the hybrid for

488
00:19:18,304 --> 00:19:21,357
the inverter alone until those details are

489
00:19:21,357 --> 00:19:22,084
published.

490
00:19:22,264 --> 00:19:24,773
Buy it because you want the extra

491
00:19:24,773 --> 00:19:27,358
power, and treat the inverter as a

492
00:19:27,358 --> 00:19:27,814
bonus.

493
00:19:28,164 --> 00:19:29,661
A word about timing.

494
00:19:29,841 --> 00:19:33,035
Toyota has not published prices or on-sale

495
00:19:33,035 --> 00:19:34,632
dates in our sources,

496
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:37,370
and the Kelley Blue Book figures are

497
00:19:37,370 --> 00:19:38,131
estimates.

498
00:19:38,311 --> 00:19:40,958
That means a careful buyer has time.

499
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:43,802
You can watch for the official numbers,

500
00:19:43,802 --> 00:19:45,646
then compare the same trim,

501
00:19:45,646 --> 00:19:47,149
with the same options,

502
00:19:47,149 --> 00:19:48,789
at more than one dealer.

503
00:19:48,969 --> 00:19:51,149
The risk of waiting is small,

504
00:19:51,149 --> 00:19:53,555
and the risk of paying a premium

505
00:19:53,555 --> 00:19:55,134
on a guess is larger.

506
00:19:55,314 --> 00:19:58,263
Patience is a form of negotiation.

507
00:19:58,613 --> 00:20:01,480
Last, who is this truck really for?

508
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:03,748
It suits a buyer who keeps a

509
00:20:03,748 --> 00:20:05,314
truck for many years,

510
00:20:05,314 --> 00:20:06,656
who values resale,

511
00:20:06,656 --> 00:20:09,042
and who is willing to verify the

512
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:10,310
engine's history.

513
00:20:10,490 --> 00:20:12,872
It suits someone who wants a hybrid

514
00:20:12,872 --> 00:20:14,982
with real power and who tows or

515
00:20:14,982 --> 00:20:15,935
works with it.

516
00:20:16,115 --> 00:20:18,512
It does not suit a buyer who

517
00:20:18,512 --> 00:20:20,396
needs certainty today,

518
00:20:20,396 --> 00:20:22,965
or who dislikes subscriptions.

519
00:20:23,145 --> 00:20:24,281
For that buyer,

520
00:20:24,281 --> 00:20:25,492
the used market,

521
00:20:25,492 --> 00:20:27,916
with a documented recall repair,

522
00:20:27,916 --> 00:20:29,658
may be the calmer path.

523
00:20:30,008 --> 00:20:32,582
A final habit worth building is to

524
00:20:32,582 --> 00:20:35,232
keep a simple folder for the truck.

525
00:20:35,412 --> 00:20:36,960
Put the window sticker,

526
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,778
the written warranty terms,

527
00:20:38,778 --> 00:20:39,922
the recall check,

528
00:20:39,922 --> 00:20:42,076
and every service receipt in it.

529
00:20:42,256 --> 00:20:44,785
If the engine ever becomes a question,

530
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:46,981
the folder answers it in minutes.

531
00:20:47,161 --> 00:20:49,391
A buyer with paperwork is in a

532
00:20:49,391 --> 00:20:52,437
very different position from a buyer with

533
00:20:52,437 --> 00:20:53,477
only a memory.

534
00:20:53,657 --> 00:20:54,959
It costs nothing,

535
00:20:54,959 --> 00:20:57,103
and for a truck with a known

536
00:20:57,103 --> 00:20:59,707
engine history, it may be the most

537
00:20:59,707 --> 00:21:01,239
useful thing you do.

538
00:21:01,589 --> 00:21:03,723
So what should you check before you

539
00:21:03,723 --> 00:21:05,919
buy a Tundra in twenty twenty-seven?

540
00:21:06,099 --> 00:21:09,380
First, the official price and the on-sale

541
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:12,020
date, once Toyota announces them.

542
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:14,970
Second, the warranty for the engine and

543
00:21:14,970 --> 00:21:16,249
the hybrid system,

544
00:21:16,249 --> 00:21:17,030
